  "problem": "Find the **exact solutions in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$",
